Wireglow for Debian 13 (trixie), amd64
====================================

Close Wireglow and let proxy recovery finish before upgrading or removing it.
The package does not stop processes or restart the application automatically.
Install or upgrade: sudo apt install ./wireglow_<version>_amd64.deb

Run Wireglow from the applications menu or with the `wireglow` command.
A graphical session and a running systemd user manager are required.
Local proxy works independently of GNOME; system proxy requires GNOME GSettings.
TUN is not implemented. No privileged helper or system service is installed.

Profiles, preferences and the proxy recovery journal keep their existing paths:
  ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/wireglow/
Runtime files use:
  ${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/<uid>}/wireglow/
User data is created at application runtime, not during package installation.
Upgrades, removal and purge leave user data intact. Back up profiles/settings
while the app is stopped; do not transfer runtime files or recovery journals
to another machine. Profiles contain credentials: keep backups private.

If an older manually registered per-user desktop entry points to another copy,
it overrides the system entry with the same application ID. Remove that stale
entry from ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/applications/ yourself if needed.
The package does not edit per-user desktop entries.

This package is unsigned. SHA-256 checksums detect accidental corruption; they
do not authenticate the publisher. There is no APT repository or auto-updater.
